---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseStudySection from "../../components/CaseStudySection.astro";

const threads = [
  {
    key: "search",
    label: "Search",
    owned: "Built Elasticsearch-backed search, ranking, filters, and result views.",
    enables: "Users can search beyond an exact title match and narrow the records they see."
  },
  {
    key: "docs",
    label: "Documentation",
    owned: "Built Markdown parsing and React rendering, connected to Directus publishing.",
    enables: "Content teams can maintain help and API guidance without editing the page implementation."
  },
  {
    key: "data",
    label: "Data quality",
    owned: "Worked with the data team to identify and correct missing and malformed records before launch.",
    enables: "Source-data issues can be fed back to the people maintaining the records."
  }
];
const mechanisms = [
  {
    thread: "search",
    layer: "Support imperfect queries",
    detail: "Fuzzy matching, ranking, and filters address the ways people actually search. An exact lookup alone would make users responsible for remembering the dataset’s naming conventions."
  },
  {
    thread: "docs",
    layer: "Separate content from its rendering",
    detail: "Markdown is parsed into an intermediate structure and rendered in React. The publishing connection lets editors change the guidance while the application owns how it appears."
  },
  {
    thread: "data",
    layer: "Check the records behind the interface",
    detail: "Record verification and feedback to data stewards sit alongside indexing work. Improving a query cannot supply a field that is missing from the source."
  }
];
const initialThread = "search";
---

<CaseStudyLayout title="Open Policy Finder" description="My work with Jisc on publishing-policy search, editable documentation, and data quality." threads={threads} initialThread={initialThread}>
  <p slot="intro">Researchers need to find the publishing policy relevant to their journal or publisher. At Jisc, I worked on the search, documentation, and data quality that help them answer that question.</p>
  <dl slot="meta" class="case-meta" aria-label="Case study summary">
    <div><dt>Context</dt><dd>Jisc / April 2023–February 2026</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Search, documentation, Elasticsearch, data quality</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Project</dt><dd><a href="https://openpolicyfinder.jisc.ac.uk">openpolicyfinder.jisc.ac.uk</a></dd></div>
  </dl>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-problem" title="Problem">
    <p>People search with partial titles, acronyms, publisher names, and imperfect recall. A relevant result also depends on the source records being complete enough to use, while the guidance needs to stay editable by the content team.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-contribution" title="My contribution">
    <table class="case-ledger">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">What I built and why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{threads.map((thread) => (
        <tr data-thread={thread.key} data-active={thread.key === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
          <th scope="row">{thread.label}</th><td><p>{thread.owned}</p><p>{thread.enables}</p></td>
        </tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-decisions" title="Decisions">
    <div class="case-prose">
      <table class="case-ledger">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Choice</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{mechanisms.map((mechanism) => (
          <tr data-thread={mechanism.thread} data-active={mechanism.thread === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
            <th scope="row">{mechanism.layer}</th><td>{mechanism.detail}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>

    </div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-result" title="What it enables">
    <div class="case-prose"><p>The work connected policy discovery with the content and data workflows behind it. My contribution covered the search and documentation implementation, alongside collaboration with the data team on record quality.</p></div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-lesson" title="Lesson">
    <p>Search quality crosses team boundaries. A confusing result might need a query change, clearer guidance, or a correction to the source record. Working through those possibilities with the people who own the data is part of building the search.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
